meta-rzg3l-fast-boot
====================

Fast-boot layer for the RZ/G3L SMARC EVK. It shortens the time from power-on to
the Weston desktop. The Weston graphics stack and the display path are not
changed.

With meta-rzg3l-seamless-logo-still, eMMC boot reaches Weston in about 6.8 s
instead of 22 s (default).

Tested with RZ/G3L BSP v1.0.0, MACHINE = "smarc-rzg3l", core-image-weston.


I. Changes
==========

  U-Boot    No boot delay. Quiet kernel command line for eMMC boot.
  Kernel    Unused peripherals are disabled in the device tree. The matching
            kernel drivers are removed.
  Distro    rz-vlp-fast: based on rz-vlp, without unused features and
            package groups.
  systemd   Unused services are masked. The journal stays in RAM. Weston
            starts without waiting for multi-user.target.


II. Build
=========

Start from the default BSP build environment (RZ/G3L Linux Start-up Guide,
2.2) and add the layer:

  $ bitbake-layers add-layer ../meta-rzg3l-fast-boot

Set in conf/local.conf:

  DISTRO = "rz-vlp-fast"

Build:

  $ MACHINE=smarc-rzg3l bitbake core-image-weston


III. Notes
==========

  - With meta-rzg3l-seamless-logo-still: add meta-rzg3l-fast-boot first.
    Both layers patch the same device tree file, in bblayers.conf order.
